  "rationale": {
    "purpose": "Implement requested elemental attacks and concrete art revisions in the existing sandbox, preserving the liked fire combo.",
    "decision_source": "User requests И fire combo binding, outward earth eruptions, actual End portal diagonal tear, VFX-only Void/Sculk; later correction requires adaptive Blockbench Bloom roots, brown thick lower roots, green pointed leaves, exact existing model+UV Pairs, independent animation for each branch and orange-to-dark magma stones. Codex chooses tick14 teleport, five wave placements, 90-tick model hold, native shader aperture runs, source-owned native OBJ bake and external layered material/cel painting. Later user explicitly requests full hostile suppression, +/-10Y eruption support with connected ground/fire VFX, visible Sculk surfaces, below40% guardian shield/resistance/golem with180degree facing correction, removal of stale-position Void targeting and all missing B utilities. Latest root steering says no further smoothing, make lower pieces chunkier. Codex chooses narrow mapped whole-action-tick pause plus native baseTick clocks/event guards, preserves old behavior outside sandbox and uses canonical local utility contracts, safe golem clearance and normal-native temporary path persistence. Latest user direction replaces Life Chorus orange stripes with natural healing/individual responses/four existing mini shields and real25% reduction; ordinary lava drinking, radial4-heart sonic V, purple teleport distance; three sequential upgrades with Bloom base3hearts then1.5hearts/second at upgradeII, full lock atI, poison once atIII. Codex chooses free ordered sandbox unlock controls, NBT respawn retention,16-block healing front preserving former healing/boons,8-block sonic radius,90tick root duration and bounded client estimate. Other race upgrades are proposals only. User supplies golden Chorus storyboard as inspiration, asks Codex to finish it independently, and requests reusable skill/prompts describing all powers. Then explicitly requests one knockback on golem entry, clarifies outward from player and also V, and asks shared code for both events. Codex chooses common16-block/12-tick/native.9 knockback wave, using V healing delay7 and immediate successful guardian trigger; per-wave UUID de-duplication, native knockback resistance, no new damage. Original built-in image_gen production sheets retain native384x256 cels and integer rune-pivot alignment, no reference crops or pixelation filter."
  },
